<title>UK: Chubb Security says in talks, may get offer.</title>
<headline>Chubb Security says in talks, may get offer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chubb Security Plc said on Thursday it was in talks that may lead to a recommended offer being made for the company.</p>
<p>&quot;Such an offer, if made, is not expected to exceed a value of 450p per share,&quot; the firm said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Chubb, which provides electronic and physical security services, said it expected to make a further announcement shortly.</p>
<p>Chubb's shares shot up more than 20 percent, gaining 76.5p to 417.5p to rank as the London Stock Exchange's top percentage gainer by 1000 GMT.</p>
<p>Earlier, a comment by the Financial Times newspaper highlighted Chubb's possible attractions to a predator, possibly from the U.S.</p>
